 2. **Migrations:** `backend/prisma/migrations/` (5 migrations through `add_report`) IS present in the GitHub snapshot audited on 2026-10-23; the earlier note saying it was missing was stale. Applying them to a real database is still unverified in the audit environment (no Postgres / Prisma engine download available) — run `npx prisma migrate deploy` against a scratch database and confirm.
 3. **New AI safeguards (see below) are verified only with stub clients.** No real OpenAI call, real Postgres run, or real Chromium render was performed for them.
 
+## Using the AI tools in the UI
+
+Each application card has an **AI tools** button (the panels load on first open).
+
+- **Tailor resume bullets** — paste your existing bullets, one per line (1–20, ≤500 characters each; the same limits the API enforces). The UI calls `POST /applications/:id/tailor` with `{ baseBullets }` and shows each result with its fact-check outcome (`accepted`, or `reverted_to_original` with the specific added numbers/terms), plus model, token counts, and the *estimated* cost the server returned. Fields the server does not return are not shown.
+- **PDF report** — requests `POST /applications/:id/report`, then polls `GET /applications/:id/report` (delays 1.5s→5s, at most 40 checks ≈ 3 minutes, sequential, cancelled on unmount). Only a server response of `done` shows the download button; the PDF is fetched with the bearer token as a blob from `/report/file`. After the polling window the UI says the status is unconfirmed and offers **Check again**. A finished report is not regenerated by the API; re-tailoring afterwards does not update an existing PDF.
+
+Frontend logic lives in `frontend/src/lib/` (pure, unit-tested) and `frontend/src/api.js`; `npm test` in `frontend/` runs those tests. The React components themselves have no automated tests yet.
+
+### Manual end-to-end check (needs Postgres, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, Inngest dev server, Playwright Chromium)
+
+1. Start the stack as in "Running it locally" (backend on :5000, `npm run inngest:dev`, frontend on :5173).
+2. Sign up, add an application with a real job description, open **AI tools**.
+3. Tailor 2–3 non-sensitive bullets; confirm bullets, fact-check notes, model/usage appear. Try a bullet that invites a fabricated metric and confirm it is reverted.
+4. Click **Generate PDF report**; confirm *Generating…* then *ready*; click **Download PDF** and open the file.
+5. Reload the page mid-generation to confirm polling resumes; stop Inngest to confirm the UI ends in *could not confirm* with **Check again**, not an endless spinner.
+6. Delete the token from localStorage (or wait for expiry) and use either panel: you should land on the login screen.
+
 ## AI safeguards (deterministic, tested with stubs)
 
 - `src/grounding.js` — after the model rewrites CV bullets, every bullet is compared with the user's original at the same index. A bullet that introduces a **new number/metric** or a **new tool/technology/proper-noun term** is **reverted to the original** and reported (`grounding[]` in the `/tailor` response; `inJobDescription: true` marks likely keyword-stuffing). Lexical only: it will not catch semantic inflation ("contributed" → "led") — the user must still review the output.
